1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,860
In Spain, one day, the calendar jumped from the 4th to

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:03,380
the 15th.

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,020
Castile, the year fifteen eighty-

4
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:06,380
two.

5
00:00:06,378 --> 00:00:10,937
Tok knocks on the door: Come in, Tok!

6
00:00:10,924 --> 00:00:12,964
It's Thursday, the fourth of October.

7
00:00:12,966 --> 00:00:15,208
Tok goes to bed without a care...

8
00:00:15,288 --> 00:00:17,288
And wakes up on Friday the fifteenth!

9
00:00:17,408 --> 00:00:19,808
No, Tok, you didn't sleep for eleven days.

10
00:00:20,128 --> 00:00:22,008
Those ten days never existed!

11
00:00:22,048 --> 00:00:22,808
Why?

12
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:25,300
Julius Caesar's calendar ran over

13
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,700
by about eleven minutes a year.

14
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:27,980
Not much...

15
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:30,660
but drip by drip, over twelve hundred years,

16
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,860
it added up to ten days.

17
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:34,140
And Easter no longer matched the

18
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:35,380
start of spring!

19
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:37,980
So Pope Gregory the Thirteenth and Philip

20
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:39,780
the Second wiped them out in one go.

21
00:00:40,127 --> 00:00:42,647
On the night of the 4th, in Alba de Tormes,

22
00:00:42,647 --> 00:00:44,407
Saint Teresa of Ávila died.

23
00:00:44,767 --> 00:00:46,407
And do you know when she was buried?

24
00:00:46,647 --> 00:00:47,847
The next day...

25
00:00:47,967 --> 00:00:49,127
which was already the 15th.

26
00:00:49,367 --> 00:00:52,047
That's why her feast day is October 15th.
